    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0469" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/598: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-06T23:00:00+03:00">August 6, 1940—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 7—9:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>979. Embassy’s telegram No. 978, August 6, 10 p.m. An understanding was reached
                    with Mikoyan to the effect that the English and Russian texts shall be
                    considered equally authentic. I left with him a note on the subject reading as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Mr. People’s Commissar, it is my understanding, which I shall be glad to
                            have you confirm to me that the English and Russian texts <pb
                                facs="0470" n="458" xml:id="pg458"/> of the exchange of notes we
                            have just effected extending the commercial agreement shall be
                            considered equally authentic.</p>
                        <p>Accept Mr. People’s Commissar the renewed assurances of my highest
                            consideration.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Mikoyan stated that he will address a note to me tomorrow confirming my
                    understanding in this matter.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d322-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d322-f1" n="73" xml:id="d322-f1-content">
                <p>The Chargé reported the receipt of this confirmation on August 7.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
